From 26bd69251fda8d110b1e646b6a5edc78fefe0cf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Romanov <romanovda@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:11:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ZDC try X8: photon cores limited to 5 layers, neutron at its
 cluster centroid, refit

Phase 4 (the Lambda bar fight), experiment X8_core_depth_centroid, build label X8, on X7 (accepted).
- ImagingTopoCluster: coreSplitCoreMaxLayer (default off): a core region keeps its hits up to that
  layer, deeper hits join the shared deep region (a photon deposits early; the neutron's energy in the
  same column is what made photon clusters impure). The ZDC uses 5 layers.
- FarForwardNeutralsReconstruction: neutronPositionCentroid (default off; set in reco.cc for the ZDC):
  the SumAll neutron and the pairing's neutron hypothesis sit at the energy-weighted centroid of their
  clusters instead of the leader cluster.
- Calibration refit on D2/D3 for this clustering: photon 3.952*E^0.938 (neutron unchanged 6.214*E^0.740).
Scans (two D4 files, X7's calibration): 847 / 867 matched at 150 / 275 GeV vs X7's 790 / 793; plateau
over 4-6 layers; the centroid alone 822 / 819 (the 471 emulation predicted 822 / 818).
Prediction: S4a_tm per thrown Lambda -> n pi0 = 7.4 % mean over 100-275 GeV and 14.0 % at 275 GeV
(X7: 6.853 % / 12.942 %). Judged against X7_core_split.
Verdict: pending (recorded in the next commit on this branch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
